A||||5||fiero56||Caliper slider lube?||||1||
Z||000000||fiero56||01-16-2000||06:56 PM||||Question is on 1988 right rear brake caliper. <BR>My "new" brake caliper finally came in Friday, and I now have a chance to install it. After much searching I was finally able to find a rebuilt caliper for $100 after an $80 core charge. Well, all I really got was a rebuilt cylinder bore assy(new seals, piston, etc). I had to transfer all external stuff onto the rebuilt one. <BR>I am now moving my old sliders and boots over to the rebuilt one and am wondering if there is any lube I should use on them, or put them in dry.<BR>If I planned on using this caliper for an extended period I would be putting in new sliders too, but I plan on doing a complete brake job this spring.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cooter||01-16-2000||07:14 PM||||There is a special grease for these sliders. I usually just use a high temp moly grease on them.||||reg||1
Z||000002||pherder||01-16-2000||07:37 PM||||Hate to post this AFTER you got your calipers BUT ...<P>You can get a pretty good price for parts (such as loaded calipers) @ CarParts.com!<P>I got brand new rotors for my 88 Coupe @ just under $50.<P>Here is an example of loaded (i.e. brake pads, etc.) rear calipers ...<P>BECK ARNLEY  Description : R RIGHT CALIPER-LOADED,# per car : 1,Year : 88  Part number : 079-5156  $ 132.75 $ 88.50 $ 90.00 <P>First price is list, 2nd is what is charged and the last price is the core charge.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by pherder (edited 01-16-2000).]||||reg||4
Z||000003||88formula||01-16-2000||08:34 PM||||You have to buy special grease for the sliders; if you use ordinary grease like bearing grease the rubber O rings will swell and cause your sliders to stick. You can use silicon grease for the sliders or synthetic grease called caliper grease sold at any auto parts store.DO NOT USE ANY OTHER GREASE.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||01-16-2000||08:48 PM||||Looks like I'll be heading out early for some caliper grease. Hope they have it in stock, nothing else ever is. <P>I had thought about ordering online, but didn't feel comfortable doing core charges with a store I'd never see. Maybe I'll get my clutch master and slave cylinders in the car tonight.||||reg||1
Z||000005||dogtired||01-17-2000||09:43 AM||||I used a White Lithium grease? Because that is what I had???  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Should I expect to have problems with it ??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><BR>What do you all think??||||reg||6
